      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s correct, we only need to call chipset_force_shutdown() once, and ovp_detect_count would be cleared after shutdown. It goes like this:\n\nt\u003d1, no OVP case \u003d\u003e GPIO_EN_PP3300\u003d1, GPIO_PP3300_PG\u003d1, ovp_detect_count\u003d 0\nt\u003d2, OVP case \u003d\u003e GPIO_EN_PP3300\u003d1, GPIO_PP3300_PG\u003d0, ovp_detect_count\u003d 1\nt\u003d3, OVP case \u003d\u003e GPIO_EN_PP3300\u003d1, GPIO_PP3300_PG\u003d0, ovp_detect_count\u003d 2\nt\u003d4, OVP case \u003d\u003e GPIO_EN_PP3300\u003d1, GPIO_PP3300_PG\u003d0, ovp_detect_count\u003d 3  \u003d\u003e force_shutdown()\nt\u003d5, shutdown \u003d\u003e GPIO_EN_PP3300\u003d0, GPIO_PP3300_PG\u003d0, ovp_detect_count\u003d 0  \u003d\u003e OVP released due to EN_PP3300 is off.",
      "parentUuid": "1d5e7e7a_892d5079",
